    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #175\n\n- 2026-09-18 05:58Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-18 06:43Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #434 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Branch `bb/relay-175-operations-04-08-provision-bootstrap-s-thr_qua57a7kx7` pushed to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #175: provisioning `/opt/semprec/shared/.env` (root:root 0600) and a companion `apns-key.p8` file as the single shared-secrets source distributed to all services via systemd `EnvironmentFile=` and Docker `env_file:`. - Added `deploy/shared/.env.example` — a values-free template covering master key, setup token, VAPID, APNs (referencing `APNS_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH`, not an inline key), AI provider/gateway secrets, OAuth, distinct DB+MinIO credentials (including the per-role `SEMPREC_API_DATABASE_URL` / `SEMPREC_SIDE_DATABASE_URL` split from issue #243), restic, and healthchecks. - `apnsAdapter.ts` now reads the APNs key from `APNS_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH` (a file) instead of an inline env value, since a multi-line PEM key has no safe representation in an `EnvironmentFile=`/`env_file:` line. - `semprec-api` and `semprec-ai-gateway` now resolve their `DATABASE_URL` from role-specific shared-env keys with backward-compatible fallback. - Documented the contract in `deploy/README.md` and `docs/operations/database-roles.md`. - `external_credentials` (user-supplied third-party secrets) stays untouched and separate, as required. Full verification suite (lint, format, build, unit/integration/e2e tests, boundary/write-safety/migration checks) passed synchronously in this branch's latest state — 1268/1268 integration tests, 410/410 unit tests, 9/9 e2e tests. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-18 06:52Z — This issue was resolved by #434, which just merged into develop.",
